update('D.2.1','Full corrected-component-count and non-Kähler-resolution obstruction proof followed.',
'proof followed; no gap found','D1.2; C3.4 independently followed',
remarks='Trivial rational H1 monodromy has coinvariant rank four, so r=s+3. This forces reducibility; the adjacent-component divisor argument rules out a compact Kähler resolution for every component of a reducible fibre.')
update('D.2.2','Full existence/sign/equality combination followed with its dependencies separated.',
'proof followed; unrestricted equality depends on remaining C2G1 chain','D2.5/7 independently followed; C2G1 global nonnegative-support theorem still has unread upstream rows',
remarks='The upper bound and the unrestricted lower bound are different inputs. Their equality gives b3=2 and each support Euler zero; the actual integral-homology example is D2.7, not a formal monodromy representation.')
update('D.2.3','Full logarithmic comparison, two positive-integral contradictions, and nonreduced ideal-subcomplex residue calculation followed.',
'proof followed; original comparison hypotheses matched','Steenbrink1976 §2.1, Theorem2.18, Proposition2.20, Theorem2.21, opened in original',
'The imported comparison is proper analytic with normal-crossing support and arbitrary multiplicities; it requires no Kähler total space. The local Koszul calculation is independently written and was rederived.',
'Identity monodromy forces zero residue and a bounded holomorphic flat frame. Nonzero branch residues force logarithmic divergence of the positive volume integral. If the generator vanishes on every branch, the J/(t) relative complex has only monomials y^a, 1<=a<gcd(m_i), hence invertible residue; equivariance kills its central class. Dividing the primitive generator by t then gives the second divergent integral. No invariant-cycle surjectivity or polarization is presumed.')
update('D.2.4','Full normalized root-cover and rational-normalization argument followed.',
'proof followed; no gap found','NC3/5; D2.3 independently followed',
remarks='The normalized multiplicity-root cover is finite etale of the smooth total space; connected generic torus fibres force connected central fibre by Stein factorization. Its normalized components cover a simply connected rational surface and hence are rational. D2.3 then contradicts identity monodromy.')
update('D.2.5','Full unrestricted positive-Euler contradiction followed, including fixed-fibre Picard jumping, multiplicity filtration, all-powers Gauduchon degree, conductor and embedded resolution.',
'proof followed; C4c dependency still tracked','C4c; A3.5; A5.2/3/6; D1.9; D2.3; analytic embedded resolution',
remarks='The proof first reduces c3>0 to b3=0. A fixed multiplicity layer carries sections for all Pic0 twists by finite analytic-union irreducibility. All positive and negative powers force every ambient pullback line to have Gauduchon degree zero. The nonempty effective conductor then gives negative canonical degree and pg=0. Every exceptional component of an embedded resolution has pg=0, so D2.3 applies without restricting multiplicities or singularities.')
update('E2','Full graph-hypersurface proof followed, including every exceptional comparison, distance-ordered divisor choice, multiplicity filtration and finite-support uniformity.',
'proof followed; known graph theorem credited','LRS2019 theorem main2 new; analytic coherence/base change; compact Gorenstein duality',
'Supplied LRS original theorem and higher-direct-image lemma opened; original CDP98 Propositions1.1/Corollary1.3 and Lemmas1.4/1.5 opened. This is the known non-holomorphic-reduction theorem with its complete proof retained.',
'The graph is the integral hypersurface av-bu=0, so its O(-1) resolution computes Rpi_*O=O directly; fibres of pi have dimension at most one. Every pencil-exceptional component dominates the target, and a full graph fibre is the corresponding Cartier divisor in Y. The auxiliary twists are chosen in reverse graph-distance order; remaining direct-image torsion is removed value by value, rather than assuming local freeness. The exceptional thickening has no higher direct image by the graph calculation. The same argument reaches every Picard component.')
update('E3','Full Moishezon intersection argument and two-independent-functions indeterminacy proof followed.',
'proof followed; exact known source numbering matched','E2 independently followed; CDP98 original Lemma1.4',
'Opened original CDP98 Lemma1.4 and its complete proof in the supplied source; it is not Corollary1.2.',
'A pushed-down ample divisor meets a pushed-down general curve with positive degree. On a six-sphere, E2 forbids an indeterminate meromorphic function; two independent holomorphic P1 maps would create one by the local quotient u/v. Thus a<=1, and any algebraic-reduction curve has genus zero.')
update('E7','Full invertible-logarithmic-period and family-by-family comparison argument followed.',
'proof followed; exact local construction source openings still tracked','E6; supplied comb periodextension/hexfill, two-parameter mum, LiuRollenske prop:compactification X',
remarks='The rank calculation is qZprime=B/(2pi i)+qHprime with det(B)!=0. Affine translations change constant data, not this leading matrix. Comb smoothing preserves the transverse Hodge graph at the cusp, giving B=I in the canonical flat frame. The result asserts a local open set of torus-fibred algebraic-dimension-one structures, not a conclusion about every deformation component.')
update('E8','Full theta heat-equation derivation, six-isogeny comparison, zero-branch derivative and exact root orders followed; E_checks.py and E_theta_numeric.py rerun successfully.',
'proof followed; exact identity and numerical consistency checks distinguished',
remarks='Recomputed the full determinant as minus the square minus wp/(4pi^2). Differentiating wp(mu,tau)=0 gives the g2/g3 expression with the stated sign. Root orders are two at the order-three point and zero after cancellation at the order-four point; the limiting cusp matrix is invertible. Two70-digit computations are consistency checks, not numerical proofs.')
update('E10','Full actual genus-two base deformation, smooth fibre product, all cohomology groups and nonzero fixed-target obstruction followed; E_checks.py and E_counterexamples.py rerun.',
'proof followed; explicit counterexample confirmed',
remarks='The disjoint Hesse critical sets keep the fibre product smooth. Moving one of six branch values while five are fixed gives nonzero base Kodaira–Spencer class. Leray gives h(O)=(1,2,6,5), h(g*TC)=(0,3,10,7), h(Trelative)=(0,6,20,14); the nonzero class lands injectively in H1(g*TC). This refutes extension to an arbitrary fixed positive-genus target, not E6 over P1.')
update('E11','Full root-pullback, tangent sequences, all-degree duality, weighted-monomial exclusion and nonzero scale Kodaira–Spencer proof followed; E_checks.py rerun.',
'proof followed; actual root construction comparison remains a source check','E7/9; Viaclovsky2026Log actual logarithmic transforms',
remarks='The root pullback sends O(1) to O(kl) but the horizontal tangent line changes to O(r+s-rs). The H3 monomial equation 3k(a+2)+4l(b+2)=kl is impossible modulo k. The489 coprime pairs k,l<=40 are bounded arithmetic checks only; the displayed argument proves the general claim. The original affine-twist computation is independent of sphere integral homology.')
update('E12','Full normalized Poincaré-line two-term complex, length-one skyscraper, fibre Tor and replacement base-change sequence followed.',
'proof followed; universal printed local-freeness claim refuted','Original CDP98 Lemma1.5 opened',
remarks='The moving degree-one section has one simple evaluation zero, so Rp_*P=C0[-1]; the P1 O(-2) factor puts it in degree two. Fibre cohomology at zero includes the degree-one Tor contribution. Local constancy of all fibre dimensions, not generic vanishing, is the valid Grauert hypothesis.')
update('E13','Full two-parameter tangent proof followed: multiplicative connection, finite-root and nodal extensions, alternating-pair identification, residue map, cross-ratio and double-curve modulus.',
'proof followed; exact two-parameter construction source matching remains','E4/7; Viaclovsky2026Two family and local models; E_checks.py rerun exit0',
remarks='The boundary dual is represented by rows(1,-b/(e_i+mu)); its determinant is b(e2-e1)/((e1+mu)(e2+mu)), nonzero because b!=0 and distinct nodal values have distinct nodes. Root cohomology gives log tangent(1,2,2,1), and the boundary plus H3=0 gives tangent(1,2,2,0). The two actual parameters have independent Kodaira–Spencer classes; the analytic inverse-function argument kills the full Kuranishi ideal, including nilpotents.')
update('E14','Full simultaneous cusp smoothing, canonical/connection extension, Hartogs pairing, free logarithmic module, nonreduced jet restriction and two independent Kodaira–Spencer directions followed.',
'proof followed; original compact construction and topology statements remain to match','E4/7/13; LiuRollenske2026 prop:surface facts and thm:main; E_checks.py rerun exit0',
remarks='The critical curve has t=-3x^2, epsilon=x^2(3+2x), so its central algebra is A=C[x]/x^2. Restriction is (a,d)->a+d(-i+ix), determinant i. Surjectivity on the reduced singular elliptic curve proves the comparison scalar is a unit; this is essential before passing to the nonreduced jet. The transverse map derivative is -1+x modulo the Jacobian ideal, whereas a global projective vector field gives a constant. Commented-out original holomorphic-invariant notes are not imported.')
update('E16','Full root-chain-rule, weighted determinant-degree and marked comb Wronskian proof followed.',
'proof followed; depends on explicit E7/13/14/15 comparison maps','E7/8/11/13/14/15',
remarks='Higher root transforms multiply the ordinary tensor by k*u^(k-1) or l*u^(l-1). For P(1,4), weighted entry orders force the root zero; the degree budget forces the stated exact nodal orders. For a specified comb, det(kappa)=y^2 P_sigma(x^4,y^3) with degree(P_sigma)=4m; no fixed defect set is assigned to an unspecified section. Source E16 has a typographic malformed text command in(E.16.3), to correct in the printed version.')
update('E17','Full embedded-point counterexample, exact stabilized-section formula, and full printed non-holomorphic proof audit followed; E_counterexamples.py rerun.',
'proof followed; exact original CDP98 claim matched; CDP20 Section3 comparison still tracked','CDP98 original Proposition1.1; LRS2019 no-embedded-component lemma and exceptional examples',
'Original CDP98 Proposition1.1 explicitly allows nonreduced spaces without excluding embedded components. Supplied LRS lemma explicitly adds that exclusion, and its exceptional-divisor examples were opened.',
'The embedded section at p survives every twist by the disjoint Cartier divisor q. For the actual resolved-pencil divisor, pullback of the P1 evaluation sequence gives R2sigma_*O(-tE)=0; this proves the required R1/R2 vanishing on tE without the false arbitrary-exceptional-divisor assertion. The graph proof computes its own higher images. The LRS adjunction sign typo does not affect the corrected full-fibre argument.')
